tation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hulsey</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Hendrickson</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Garc&#x000ed;a de Le&#x000f3;n</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trophic morphology, feeding performance, and prey use in the polymorphic fish <italic>Herichthys minckleyi</italic></article-title><source>Evolutionary Ecology Research</source><year>2005</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>303</fpage><lpage>324</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kornfield</surname><given-names>IL</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>JN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A new species of polymorphic fish, <italic>Cichlasoma minckleyi</italic>, from Cuatro Ci&#x000e9;negas, Mexico (Teleostei: Cichlidae)</article-title><source>Proceedings of the Biological Society of Washington</source><year>1983</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>253</fpage><lpage>269</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>DeWitt</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>BW</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Functional diversity among predators of a freshwater snail imposes an adaptive trade-off for shell morphology</article-title><source>Evolutionary Ecology Research</source><year>2000</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>129</fpage><lpage>148</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rundle</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Bronmark</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inter- and intr